From: REG-Linux <dev@reglinux.org>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: cha: adjust model, disable ethernet, cap OPPs

Rename the board model string to "Capcom Home Arcade".

The Capcom Home Arcade (CHA) board has no Ethernet PHY populated. The
inherited LibreTech DTS enables it, causing an EMAC reset timeout and
PHY probe failure at boot. Disable the ethernet node.

The CHA's Type-A USB port is used exclusively in host mode for pen drive
access. MTP/ADB gadget mode is not supported on CHA because the MUSB-sunxi
driver's suspend/resume path is broken upstream and MTP sessions drop every
time the host autosuspends the bus. The LibreTech DTSI already sets
dr_mode = "host" on the OTG port, which is what CHA needs - nothing to
override for USB.

The CHA vdd-cpux is a fixed 1.2V regulator. OPPs above 1008 MHz require
1.32-1.40V and are silently rejected by the OPP framework at boot, generating
spurious error messages. Mark them disabled so the framework skips them.

---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h3-libretech-all-h3-cc.dts | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h3-libretech-all-h3-cc.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-h3-libretech-all-h3-cc.dts
@@ -9,6 +9,28 @@
 #include "sunxi-libretech-all-h3-cc.dtsi"

 / {
-	model = "Libre Computer Board ALL-H3-CC H3";
+	model = "Capcom Home Arcade";
 	compatible = "libretech,all-h3-cc-h3", "allwinner,sun8i-h3";
 };
+
+/* CHA: no Ethernet PHY populated on this board */
+&emac {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+/* CHA: vdd-cpux is a fixed 1.2V regulator; OPPs requiring >1.3V are unreachable */
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1104000000} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1200000000} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1296000000} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&{/opp-table-cpu/opp-1368000000} {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
